//
// Description : PROTOTYPE of a library host class: a cFTLocalWebControlHost laid out on a grid of 8 px
//               columns the way a Windows dialog is - controls at their size, the extra space where it
//               stretches.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg

/* THE GRID HOST - a prototype, to move into the library once it holds up.

   Laid out the way a Windows dialog is (Nils 2026-09-27: "we are really building a Windows
   application"), with his fine-grained width knob kept (2026-09-28): the columns are a FIXED 8 px, so a
   control's piColumnSpan is its width in 8 px steps and piColumnIndex its place, much like dialog units
   - the same at any window size.

   - peLayoutType ltGrid: a control sits in a column AND a row - piColumnIndex and piRowIndex (both
     count from 0), piColumnSpan and piRowSpan.
   - psDefaultColumnWidth "8px": every column is 8 px unless psColumnWidths says otherwise.
   - psDefaultRowHeight: a row is as tall as its tallest control, and never less than one FT row
     (--ft-row), so an empty row keeps the height of a row of buttons.

   The object says where the window stretches: psColumnWidths "43/1fr" gives column 43 the extra width
   (an empty column between the left and right groups, or under a field that grows); psRowHeights
   "1/1fr" gives row 1 the extra height (a page or a list, with pbFillHeight). Never percentages: they
   are a share of the WHOLE height and ignore the other rows. A width entry past piColumnCount is
   ignored.

   The host must be at least as wide as its fixed columns add up to, at the window's MINIMUM size - so
   piColumnCount follows each host's width: (its narrowest width in px) / 8, plus the stretching column.
   A caption longer than its span is cut off, as in a Windows dialog: size the control to its caption.

   The grid trap: piColumnSpan 0 means ONE column here, not "the rest of the row" as in the flow
   layout - a control that spans the width says how many columns.

   The OverrideProperty tags tell the Studio these are the class's own defaults, so its Designer and
   property panel show them; the Sets make them so at run time. */
{ OverrideProperty=peLayoutType InitialValue=ltGrid }
{ OverrideProperty=psDefaultColumnWidth InitialValue="8px" }
Class cDemoGridHost is a cFTLocalWebControlHost
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        Set peLayoutType to ltGrid
        Set psDefaultColumnWidth to "8px"
        Set psDefaultRowHeight to "minmax(var(--ft-row, 33px), max-content)"
    End_Procedure
End_Class
